86 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 60 0 R
/T (The major components interact in a request/response style driven by a single coordinating component. The user interacts only with the Simulation UI, which forwards commands \(such as adding a vehicle\) to the Simulation Controller. The Simulation Controller is the mediator: it does not itself hold traffic-domain logic, but delegates to the Vehicle Manager \(vehicle creation and lifecycle\), the Signal Controller \(Red/Yellow/Green state per lane\), the Congestion Detector, and the Statistics Manager, and relays their results back to the Simulation UI for display. This keeps any single component small and focused, which matters for a data- structures-driven course project where the Queue Manager itself is meant to be the centrepiece.)
/E (The major components interact in a request/response style driven by a single coordinating component. The user interacts only with the Simulation UI, which forwards commands \(such as adding a vehicle\) to the Simulation Controller. The Simulation Controller is the mediator: it does not itself hold traffic-domain logic, but delegates to the Vehicle Manager \(vehicle creation and lifecycle\), the Signal Controller \(Red/Yellow/Green state per lane\), the Congestion Detector, and the Statistics Manager, and relays their results back to the Simulation UI for display. This keeps any single component small and focused, which matters for a data- structures-driven course project where the Queue Manager itself is meant to be the centrepiece.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
